WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:03.000
-Donald Trump reappeared
on Fox News

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:04.234
for the first time in six months

00:00:04.234 --> 00:00:06.133
as he faces
an expected indictment

00:00:06.133 --> 00:00:08.767
and ratchets up his attacks on
Florida governor Ron DeSantis,

00:00:08.767 --> 00:00:11.167
and Fox, which has
tied itself politically

00:00:11.167 --> 00:00:12.534
and financially to Trump,

00:00:12.534 --> 00:00:15.901
is clearly torn between
the MAGA base they helped create

00:00:15.901 --> 00:00:17.901
and which are desperately
afraid of losing

00:00:17.901 --> 00:00:20.100
and their desire
to pivot toward DeSantis,

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:21.434
which doesn't seem
to be working.

00:00:21.434 --> 00:00:23.734
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:23.734 --> 00:00:25.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:27.968 --> 00:00:30.534
Donald Trump has once again
overtaken the news cycle.

00:00:30.534 --> 00:00:31.801
So just in case
you've forgotten,

00:00:31.801 --> 00:00:33.701
it's worth remembering
that he is

00:00:33.701 --> 00:00:35.667
and has always been
deeply unpopular,

00:00:35.667 --> 00:00:37.100
and a large majority
of Americans

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:38.467
just want him to go away.

00:00:38.467 --> 00:00:40.400
They've said so in three
straight national elections

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:42.234
and over and over again
in countless polls.

00:00:42.234 --> 00:00:44.400
Personally, my solution
would be to put him

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:47.100
in a DeLorean with Doc Brown,
send him back to the year 1946,

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:48.834
stop his parents
from conceiving him,

00:00:48.834 --> 00:00:50.701
and then nuke
that [bleep] clock tower

00:00:50.701 --> 00:00:53.200
so he can't make his way back --
problem solved.

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:54.434
One day we'll just wake up

00:00:54.434 --> 00:00:56.033
and he would start
magically disappearing

00:00:56.033 --> 00:00:58.767
from photos like Marty McFly.

00:00:58.767 --> 00:01:02.200
Remember that when he posed
with a can of beans?

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:04.634
There are so many pictures
where removing Donald Trump

00:01:04.634 --> 00:01:07.033
makes it impossible to believe
the missing element

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:09.734
is a former president.

00:01:09.734 --> 00:01:11.667
I mean, he was in this picture
with Kid Rock.

00:01:11.667 --> 00:01:13.534
That was a president picture.

00:01:13.534 --> 00:01:15.167
He was in this picture
with a glowing orb.

00:01:15.167 --> 00:01:16.501
That was a president pic--

00:01:16.501 --> 00:01:18.267
He was in this picture
with the shocked Easter Bunny.

00:01:18.267 --> 00:01:20.834
He was --
A president was there.

00:01:20.834 --> 00:01:23.234
Trump must have been so mad
when he saw they got him

00:01:23.234 --> 00:01:24.467
an Easter Bunny with glasses.

00:01:24.467 --> 00:01:27.367
[ As Trump ] He's a nerd.
I'm not...

00:01:27.367 --> 00:01:30.667
taking a picture
with a nerd rabbit.

00:01:30.667 --> 00:01:32.000
[ Normal voice ]
Trump's deep unpopularity

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:34.200
was proven yet again
in another poll out this week

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:35.367
where a large majority said

00:01:35.367 --> 00:01:37.634
they do not want him
re-elected president.

00:01:37.634 --> 00:01:40.801
And even worse for Trump,
the bad news came from Fox.

00:01:40.801 --> 00:01:44.534
-61% of people do not want
former President Trump

00:01:44.534 --> 00:01:45.767
to be elected again.

00:01:45.767 --> 00:01:47.067
-I mean, that's amazing.

00:01:47.067 --> 00:01:49.434
61% are already
a hard no on Trump.

00:01:49.434 --> 00:01:52.434
And it's not like he can say,
"Yeah, it's 61% now,

00:01:52.434 --> 00:01:53.934
but wait until
they get to know me."

00:01:53.934 --> 00:01:57.167
We [bleep] know you, dude.

00:01:57.167 --> 00:02:01.200
We got to see you do the job
we don't want you to have again.

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:02.467
I mean, we can find someone else

00:02:02.467 --> 00:02:04.467
to yell at the kid
mowing the White House lawn.

00:02:04.467 --> 00:02:07.067
Oh, that's another good example.

00:02:07.067 --> 00:02:09.501
[ Laughter ]

00:02:09.501 --> 00:02:10.534
It was a president.

00:02:10.534 --> 00:02:12.801
That was a picture
of a president.

00:02:12.801 --> 00:02:14.167
But that's the problem
for Republicans.

00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:16.234
Trump is deeply unpopular
with the majority of Americans

00:02:16.234 --> 00:02:19.000
while also remaining
very popular with the GOP base.

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:22.801
One new poll out this week gave
Trump a 26-point national lead

00:02:22.801 --> 00:02:24.467
over Florida governor
Ron DeSantis

00:02:24.467 --> 00:02:27.834
and another show that Trump
has actually added to his lead

00:02:27.834 --> 00:02:29.868
with a 15-point gain
since December,

00:02:29.868 --> 00:02:31.667
while DeSantis
has dropped 12 points.

00:02:31.667 --> 00:02:33.534
And that increase
has coincided with Trump

00:02:33.534 --> 00:02:36.133
stepping up his attacks
on DeSantis on social media,

00:02:36.133 --> 00:02:37.901
at his rallies, and on Fox News.

00:02:37.901 --> 00:02:40.133
In an interview with
Sean Hannity on Monday night,

00:02:40.133 --> 00:02:41.567
Trump laid into DeSantis

00:02:41.567 --> 00:02:44.067
and claimed his political career
would be dead

00:02:44.067 --> 00:02:46.501
without Trump's endorsement
back in 2018.

00:02:46.501 --> 00:02:48.801
-So what happened with Ron
is the following.

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:50.133
He came to see me.

00:02:50.133 --> 00:02:52.334
He was getting killed.
He was being crushed.

00:02:52.334 --> 00:02:55.567
Ron came to see me,
tears in his eyes.

00:02:55.567 --> 00:02:58.100
He said, "I need you
to do me a big favor."

00:02:58.100 --> 00:03:02.000
First he asked for the meeting,
then he asked me for the favor.

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:04.200
I said, "What's the favor?"

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:05.634
"Would you endorse me?"

00:03:05.634 --> 00:03:08.601
He said,
"I need your endorsement."

00:03:08.601 --> 00:03:10.968
I said, "Ron,
you're so far behind,

00:03:10.968 --> 00:03:14.968
I can't imagine that if you got
George Washington's endorsement

00:03:14.968 --> 00:03:18.734
combined with the great --
late great Abraham Lincoln,

00:03:18.734 --> 00:03:20.701
if you had their endorsements,
I don't think you could win,

00:03:20.701 --> 00:03:23.033
Ron, but tell me about it,
go ahead."

00:03:23.033 --> 00:03:24.901
He said, "I'm telling you,
I think I could win

00:03:24.901 --> 00:03:26.267
if I could get
your endorsement."

00:03:26.267 --> 00:03:28.300
-Alright, first of all,
why is George Washington

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:29.534
just George Washington

00:03:29.534 --> 00:03:33.701
but Abraham Lincoln
is the late great Abraham?

00:03:33.701 --> 00:03:36.400
I'm certain that's the extent
of Trump's knowledge

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:37.501
about Abraham Lincoln.

00:03:37.501 --> 00:03:38.968
If you asked him
to say anything else,

00:03:38.968 --> 00:03:40.567
it would just turn
into word soup.

00:03:40.567 --> 00:03:42.601
[ As Trump ] Abraham Lincoln,
he was definitely great,

00:03:42.601 --> 00:03:44.701
and he is definitely late,
AKA dead.

00:03:44.701 --> 00:03:46.300
He died.

00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:47.567
He died so tragically

00:03:47.567 --> 00:03:51.767
when John Wilkes
jumped out of a phone booth...

00:03:51.767 --> 00:03:53.334
and said, "Your hat
or your life."

00:03:53.334 --> 00:03:55.033
But Lincoln, he couldn't
take off his hat.

00:03:55.033 --> 00:03:56.567
People don't know that.

00:03:56.567 --> 00:03:59.000
He couldn't take off his hat
because it was a stovepipe

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:01.167
and therefore hot to the touch.

00:04:01.167 --> 00:04:03.033
[ Laughter ]

00:04:05.367 --> 00:04:06.601
[ Normal voice ]
Trump then continued

00:04:06.601 --> 00:04:08.234
with his attacks on DeSantis.

00:04:08.234 --> 00:04:10.367
-I said, "Let's give it a shot,
Ron, okay?"

00:04:10.367 --> 00:04:12.634
And he was desperate.

00:04:12.634 --> 00:04:15.434
I said, "Okay."
I gave him a nice endorsement.

00:04:15.434 --> 00:04:17.434
I said, "You write out what
you'd like and let me see it."

00:04:17.434 --> 00:04:19.033
He wrote it out.
I thought it was terrible.

00:04:19.033 --> 00:04:23.167
I changed it, made it great.
I gave him a great endorsement.

00:04:23.167 --> 00:04:26.033
From the moment
I pressed that button,

00:04:26.033 --> 00:04:27.167
he blew the guy away.

00:04:27.167 --> 00:04:28.334
The race was over.

00:04:28.334 --> 00:04:30.033
And I said, "Ron,
you can beat this guy.

00:04:30.033 --> 00:04:31.300
Let's go."

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:32.734
I got him the nomination.

00:04:32.734 --> 00:04:34.868
By the way, could have never
gotten the nomination.

00:04:34.868 --> 00:04:37.400
He would be working in either
a pizza parlor place

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:39.834
or a law office right now.

00:04:39.834 --> 00:04:41.567
-You know Trump is a New Yorker

00:04:41.567 --> 00:04:43.467
because the only two professions
he can think of

00:04:43.467 --> 00:04:45.734
are pizza parlor and law office.

00:04:45.734 --> 00:04:47.067
[ Laughter ]

00:04:47.067 --> 00:04:48.234
Although Trump has clearly

00:04:48.234 --> 00:04:50.667
never been inside
a pizza place himself,

00:04:50.667 --> 00:04:54.133
given that he refers to it
as a "pizza parlor place."

00:04:54.133 --> 00:04:55.767
[ Laughter ]

00:04:55.767 --> 00:04:57.334
Sounds like a Russian spy

00:04:57.334 --> 00:05:00.667
whose submarine ran aground
on Staten Island.

00:05:00.667 --> 00:05:02.934
[ Russian accent ] Where is
your nearest pizza parlor place?

00:05:02.934 --> 00:05:05.734
My stomach is barking
like dog mouth,

00:05:05.734 --> 00:05:09.334
and I could consume
multiple triangle slices.

00:05:09.334 --> 00:05:10.834
[ Laughter ]

00:05:10.834 --> 00:05:13.200
Triangle is most
delicious shape.

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:14.834
[ Laughter ]

00:05:14.834 --> 00:05:17.367
[ Normal voice ]
So Trump is trashing DeSantis,

00:05:17.367 --> 00:05:19.701
which has apparently
been helping him in
GOP primary polls,

00:05:19.701 --> 00:05:21.300
even though he's still
incredibly unpopular

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:22.534
with the rest of the electorate.

00:05:22.534 --> 00:05:24.067
And that's the inherent
problem for Fox News.

00:05:24.067 --> 00:05:25.434
They helped create this monster,

00:05:25.434 --> 00:05:28.100
and now, seeing that it's been
a catastrophic failure,

00:05:28.100 --> 00:05:29.767
they've been trying
to tiptoe away from Trump.

00:05:29.767 --> 00:05:31.667
But their viewers,
the Trump base, won't have it.

00:05:31.667 --> 00:05:33.300
It's like the story
of Frankenstein's monster,

00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:34.434
except in this version,

00:05:34.434 --> 00:05:37.601
the villagers [bleep]
love the monster.

00:05:37.601 --> 00:05:40.033
"Hey, you're the monster.
Dude, I love your work.

00:05:40.033 --> 00:05:42.834
Would you sign my pitchfork?"

00:05:42.834 --> 00:05:44.801
That's why Fox originally
tried to ditch Trump

00:05:44.801 --> 00:05:47.234
after the 2020 election
and subsequent coup attempt

00:05:47.234 --> 00:05:48.467
but then turned around
and embraced

00:05:48.467 --> 00:05:49.968
his insane conspiracy theories,

00:05:49.968 --> 00:05:53.334
even though they knew they were
insane and said so in private.

00:05:53.334 --> 00:05:55.167
Rupert Murdoch wrote
in an e-mail

00:05:55.167 --> 00:05:57.567
after the insurrection
that Fox host Sean Hannity

00:05:57.567 --> 00:05:59.767
had been "privately disgusted
by Trump for weeks,

00:05:59.767 --> 00:06:01.267
but was scared to lose viewers."

00:06:01.267 --> 00:06:04.334
And after the election,
Hannity sent a text that said...

00:06:06.033 --> 00:06:07.033
They were so scared.

00:06:07.033 --> 00:06:08.300
I can only imagine

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:10.267
what Hannity was doing
when he sent that text.

00:06:10.267 --> 00:06:12.100
He was probably
lying on the floor

00:06:12.100 --> 00:06:13.801
watching election returns
with...

00:06:13.801 --> 00:06:15.000
-Tears in his eyes.

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:17.901
-But that's the modern
conservative movement

00:06:17.901 --> 00:06:19.167
in a microcosm right there.

00:06:19.167 --> 00:06:20.567
Donald Trump's
twisted relationship

00:06:20.567 --> 00:06:22.734
with the most powerful
right-wing propaganda outlet

00:06:22.734 --> 00:06:25.567
in the country, Fox News, has
been a decade-long soap opera

00:06:25.567 --> 00:06:27.801
that the rest of us
have sadly had to live with,

00:06:27.801 --> 00:06:30.067
despite the fact
that everyone involved sucks.

00:06:30.067 --> 00:06:33.067
It's very much an
"Alien vs. Predator" situation

00:06:33.067 --> 00:06:34.901
where sometimes the alien
and the predator are friends,

00:06:34.901 --> 00:06:36.701
sometimes the alien
and the predator bicker,

00:06:36.701 --> 00:06:39.400
but mostly the alien
has a huge MAGA fan base --

00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:42.200
make aliens great again --
that the Predator News network

00:06:42.200 --> 00:06:44.367
is desperately afraid of losing,
and the alien knows that.

00:06:44.367 --> 00:06:45.968
So anytime he doesn't like
the coverage he's getting

00:06:45.968 --> 00:06:47.834
from the Predator channel,
he does a rally

00:06:47.834 --> 00:06:49.634
where he complains
about their anti-alien bias.

00:06:49.634 --> 00:06:52.868
That explains why when I turned
into Trump's rally on Saturday,

00:06:52.868 --> 00:06:54.467
he sounded like this.

00:06:54.467 --> 00:06:56.467
[ Alien screeching ]

00:06:59.367 --> 00:07:02.534
[ Laughter ]

00:07:02.534 --> 00:07:04.734
Fox has put themselves
in a situation

00:07:04.734 --> 00:07:06.934
where they've tied their
financial and political success

00:07:06.934 --> 00:07:09.300
to Trump and his base,
a base they helped create.

00:07:09.300 --> 00:07:12.367
But now that Trump is under
multiple criminal investigations

00:07:12.367 --> 00:07:13.634
and has tanked the GOP

00:07:13.634 --> 00:07:15.634
in those three successive
national elections,

00:07:15.634 --> 00:07:19.033
Fox is gently trying to nudge
their audience toward DeSantis

00:07:19.033 --> 00:07:20.200
without pissing them off.

00:07:20.200 --> 00:07:22.734
For example,
after Trump attacked DeSantis,

00:07:22.734 --> 00:07:23.868
Fox host Brian Kilmeade

00:07:23.868 --> 00:07:25.300
criticized Trump
the next morning.

00:07:25.300 --> 00:07:28.267
-With Ron DeSantis,
he sees a threat,

00:07:28.267 --> 00:07:31.167
but I think that his best
offense as the front-runner

00:07:31.167 --> 00:07:32.834
would be don't punch down.

00:07:32.834 --> 00:07:35.434
-All Donald Trump knows
is punching down.

00:07:35.434 --> 00:07:36.968
Telling Trump not to punch down
would be like

00:07:36.968 --> 00:07:39.300
telling Don Rickles
not to antagonize the audience.

00:07:39.300 --> 00:07:41.834
Sorry, the late great
Don Rickles.

00:07:41.834 --> 00:07:45.501
One half of the comedy duo
Rickles and Lincoln.

00:07:45.501 --> 00:07:46.834
[ Laughter ]

00:07:46.834 --> 00:07:48.868
Then there was Fox personality
Jason Chaffetz,

00:07:48.868 --> 00:07:51.701
who didn't like how much Trump
whined during the interview.

00:07:51.701 --> 00:07:54.067
-Jason, you said overall,
you thought President Trump

00:07:54.067 --> 00:07:55.834
did a very poor job
in the interview.

00:07:55.834 --> 00:07:58.200
Why?

00:07:58.200 --> 00:08:01.000
-I thought Sean Hannity
did a good job,

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:02.267
but I watched that
and I thought,

00:08:02.267 --> 00:08:03.734
"Where is Donald Trump?"

00:08:03.734 --> 00:08:05.834
I voted for Donald Trump twice.

00:08:05.834 --> 00:08:08.601
I have defended him
countless times.

00:08:08.601 --> 00:08:10.100
I thought he was horrific.

00:08:10.100 --> 00:08:12.033
I think that was
the worst interview

00:08:12.033 --> 00:08:13.267
I've seen the president do.

00:08:13.267 --> 00:08:16.501
He was whining.
He was complaining.

00:08:16.501 --> 00:08:20.234
He played the victim card
time and time again.

00:08:20.234 --> 00:08:22.501
And then after that,
he complained

00:08:22.501 --> 00:08:24.634
that, you know,
somebody he had endorsed

00:08:24.634 --> 00:08:26.133
was now running against him.

00:08:26.133 --> 00:08:29.200
And I thought he was
absolutely horrific.

00:08:29.200 --> 00:08:32.501
He's the former president
of the United States.

00:08:32.501 --> 00:08:35.167
Act like it.
He didn't in that interview.

00:08:35.167 --> 00:08:36.968
-I'm sorry. Which Donald Trump
were you expecting?

00:08:36.968 --> 00:08:38.734
The Donald Trump who whines,
complains,

00:08:38.734 --> 00:08:40.033
and plays the victim card

00:08:40.033 --> 00:08:42.267
or the Donald Trump
who doesn't [bleep] exist

00:08:42.267 --> 00:08:46.567
because there's only
the first one?

00:08:46.567 --> 00:08:49.234
He's got two shticks, punching
down and playing the victim.

00:08:49.234 --> 00:08:51.200
That's it.
That's the whole deal.

00:08:51.200 --> 00:08:53.667
And as much as the rest of us
hate it, for Republican voters,

00:08:53.667 --> 00:08:55.033
that's not a negative for Trump.

00:08:55.033 --> 00:08:57.501
That's why he's
the GOP front-runner.

00:08:57.501 --> 00:08:59.167
Either these guys
still don't get it

00:08:59.167 --> 00:09:00.634
or they're just pretending
not to get it

00:09:00.634 --> 00:09:03.100
because they don't want to admit
that they've devoted their lives

00:09:03.100 --> 00:09:06.167
to a morally and ideologically
bankrupt political movement

00:09:06.167 --> 00:09:07.734
whose main goals
are cutting taxes,

00:09:07.734 --> 00:09:09.267
making it easier
for people to get guns,

00:09:09.267 --> 00:09:10.601
and losing their [bleep]
over the fact

00:09:10.601 --> 00:09:12.534
that the green M&amp;M doesn't
give them a boner anymore.

00:09:12.534 --> 00:09:17.100
The only genuine belief
Donald Trump has,

00:09:17.100 --> 00:09:20.167
as far as I can tell,
is that democracy is for losers

00:09:20.167 --> 00:09:22.634
and some form of dictatorship
would be much better.

00:09:22.634 --> 00:09:24.868
He basically came out
and said as much

00:09:24.868 --> 00:09:25.968
in the second part
of his interview

00:09:25.968 --> 00:09:27.200
with Hannity last night.

00:09:27.200 --> 00:09:30.100
Trump praised
China's totalitarian regime

00:09:30.100 --> 00:09:32.133
when he was asked
if presidential candidates

00:09:32.133 --> 00:09:34.000
should have to take
a cognitive test.

00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:36.167
-I'd like to see it for
anybody running for president.

00:09:36.167 --> 00:09:37.934
I think somebody
running for president

00:09:37.934 --> 00:09:40.634
taking a cognitive test --
You know, they do it in China.

00:09:40.634 --> 00:09:42.767
But it's done a different way.

00:09:42.767 --> 00:09:45.467
They have a caste system.

00:09:45.467 --> 00:09:47.868
And the smartest person
gets to the top.

00:09:47.868 --> 00:09:51.467
-First of all, that's definitely
not how a caste system works.

00:09:51.467 --> 00:09:53.400
[ Laughter ]

00:09:53.400 --> 00:09:55.267
Even when he's saying
he should get the job

00:09:55.267 --> 00:09:58.901
because he's smarter,
he's dumb as [bleep]

00:09:58.901 --> 00:10:04.434
No one who's actually smart
has to explain a caste system

00:10:04.434 --> 00:10:06.033
by doing this with their hands.

00:10:06.033 --> 00:10:07.367
He looks like he's playing

00:10:07.367 --> 00:10:09.367
one of those
rhyming games for children.

00:10:09.367 --> 00:10:11.501
[ As Trump ] Here's the church,
here's the steeple,

00:10:11.501 --> 00:10:16.234
here's the caste system
with all the smartest people.

00:10:16.234 --> 00:10:19.200
That's how it works, Sean.

00:10:19.200 --> 00:10:21.300
[ Normal voice ]
Fox and the conservative
movement created a monster,

00:10:21.300 --> 00:10:22.901
and now they're trying
to free themselves from it.

00:10:22.901 --> 00:10:24.033
But so far, it's not working.

00:10:24.033 --> 00:10:25.601
Trump is the star
of a political movement

00:10:25.601 --> 00:10:27.767
that they built,
a movement built on victimhood,

00:10:27.767 --> 00:10:29.901
persecution, and wanting
to have sex with M&amp;M's.

00:10:29.901 --> 00:10:31.167
And as we all know,

00:10:31.167 --> 00:10:33.000
when it comes to having sex
with an M&amp;M...

00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:35.067
-The smartest person
gets to the top.

00:10:35.067 --> 00:10:37.000
[ Laughter ]

00:10:41.434 --> 00:10:44.067
-During the commercial,
let's all think about that.

00:10:44.067 --> 00:10:46.234
[ Laughter ]
This has been "A Closer Look."

00:10:46.234 --> 00:10:48.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

